From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:23:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Merge request line 6: a pin-only layer PR's green check
 judged nothing

Owner rule, 2026-11-07 (six-line merge request), and a finding the same day:
who-iris#190's "No new failures" job 128355317559 passed but ran nothing,
because layer CI mounts the root's lock, not the caller's. A pin-only layer
PR's line 6 now says so, and the evidence for its pins is the root's re-pin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPfGantMCt7AV4LCCK2
---
 sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-manager-watcher.md | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-manager-watcher.md b/sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-manager-watcher.md
index f5e4300..8a40090 100644
--- a/sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-manager-watcher.md
+++ b/sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/merge-manager-watcher.md
@@ -163,7 +163,11 @@ chat then ask to merge by card". A sibling's `ready:` message carries:
    preview, or the layer's equivalent), confirmed rendered, or
    `no preview: <reason>`;
 5. what to look for in the preview;
-6. `full tier green as judged` (rule 1 below).
+6. `full tier green as judged` (rule 1 below). For a pin-only PR in a layer
+   repository, line 6 reads `pin-only: layer CI judges nothing (it mounts the
+   root's lock)`, because its "No new failures" job runs no tests or gates and
+   passes without judging anything. The evidence for those pins is the root's
+   own re-pin PR, not the layer's green check.
 
 The merge manager posts all six lines in its chat, then asks the owner by
 card. A request with no rendered preview and no reason goes back to the
